EXT. ANDEAN CABLE GONDOLA - DUSK

A two-seat steel gondola hangs motionless over a ravine. Wind rocks it. Below, a river thunders through black rock.

INT. CABLE GONDOLA - CONTINUOUS

Cramped. Fogged glass. RAMONA QUISPE (40s, mountain guide, cracked lip, orange windbreaker) wedges herself in a corner with a radio. EDMUND "ED" BAYLISS (60s, retired surveyor, tweed jacket, knee brace) grips the seat with both hands.

RAMONA
Base, Base, this is Quispe in cabin six. Over.

Static. Ed stares at the floor.

ED
Do not tell me we've lost the line.

RAMONA
Quiet, please.

RESCUE COORDINATOR (V.O.)
(radio, crackling)
Cabin six, we read you. Say your count.

RAMONA
Two. One guide, one passenger. No injuries.

RESCUE COORDINATOR (V.O.)
Copy. Cable crew is ninety minutes out. Snow on the access road.

Ed exhales, long and shaky.

ED
Ninety minutes.

RAMONA
It's good news, Ed. It means they're coming.

ED
I know what it means. I've been wrong about distances my whole life.

The gondola lurches. Both of them stiffen. It settles. Ed pries open a thermos with trembling fingers.

RESCUE COORDINATOR (V.O.)
Quispe, confirm you have warm layers.

RAMONA
Confirm. Emergency blanket, two.

She tears open a foil packet and drapes one over Ed's shoulders. He tries to refuse. She tucks it tight.

ED
You'd make a decent nurse.

RAMONA
I'd make a terrible nurse. I make a good guide.

Silence. Wind. The glass rattles faintly.

ED
Do you ever get used to it? The height?

RAMONA
No. You learn which fear is worth listening to.

ED
And this one?

RAMONA
This one is just cold.

Ed laughs, surprised. Ramona half smiles. The radio crackles again.

RESCUE COORDINATOR (V.O.)
Cabin six, new estimate, seventy-five minutes. Road crew cleared the slide.

RAMONA
Copy, seventy-five.

ED
That's a fifteen-minute improvement.

RAMONA
It's a fifteen-minute improvement.

She lowers the radio. The dark outside deepens. Ed pulls the blanket around himself, and Ramona settles her back against the cold glass.

ED
Tell me about the mountain.

RAMONA
Which one?

ED
Any of them.

RAMONA
My grandfather said they listen. If you say their name wrong, they send weather.

ED
What did you call this one?

RAMONA
Apu Kuntur.

ED
(trying it)
Apu Kuntur.

A gust shakes the cabin. Then the wind drops, and the whole gondola goes still.

ED (CONT'D)
Well. Perhaps I said it right.

RAMONA
Perhaps.

RESCUE COORDINATOR (V.O.)
Cabin six, I'm hearing you laughing. That's what I like to hear.

RAMONA
(to the radio)
Just keep coming.
